.TH CRS\-SCREEN 1 "2026-11-20" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-screen \- open Mu2e control room screens from a remote control room
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remote\-site/crs\-screen
.B \-\-site
.I NAME
.IR SESSION " ..."
.br
.B remote\-site/crs\-screen
.B \-\-site
.I NAME
.B \-\-check
.RI [ SESSION " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each
.IR SESSION ,
.B crs\-screen
gets a Kerberos ticket if there is none (from the site keytab), then runs
.B crs\-tunnel connect
with the site overlay
.BR remote\-site/sites/ \fINAME\fB.yaml ,
the site's VNC viewer and saved password files.
Whether the viewer is view\-only comes from the overlay.
It never starts or stops anything on the DAQ hosts.
Launchers made by
.B remote\-site/install.sh
run this command in a terminal window; on errors the window stays open
until Enter is pressed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-site " NAME"
Site whose files in
.B remote\-site/sites/
to use (default:
.BR CRS_REMOTE_SITE ).
.TP
.B \-\-check
Do not open screens. Get a ticket, then make one
.B "ssh \-J"
login per distinct host for the given sessions (all, if none given),
interactively, so host\-key questions are answered; print PASS or FAIL.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_REMOTE_SITE
Default site.
.TP
.B DRY_RUN
If set, print the commands and change nothing.
.TP
.B CRS_NO_PAUSE
If set, do not wait for Enter after an error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI remote\-site/sites/ NAME .yaml
Site overlay for
.BR crs\-tunnel (1).
.TP
.BI remote\-site/sites/ NAME .env
Launcher settings: SITE_PRINCIPAL, SITE_KEYTAB, SITE_VIEWER,
SITE_PASSWORD_FILE, SITE_LAUNCHERS.
.TP
.BI ~/.config/mu2edaq\-remote\-site/ NAME .env
Machine\-local overrides, read after the site file.
.TP
.B ~/.crs/tunnels.log ", " ~/.crs/viewer\-*.log
Output of the tunnel ssh processes and of each viewer.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
    remote\-site/crs\-screen \-\-site caltech \-\-check
    remote\-site/crs\-screen \-\-site caltech shift\-main cr01
    DRY_RUN=1 remote\-site/crs\-screen \-\-site caltech dcs\-main
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-nodes (1),
.BR crs\-tunnel (1),
.B remote\-site/README.md
